  "definition": "Transaction Processing encompasses the end-to-end lifecycle of blockchain transactions \u2014 from cryptographic signing and mempool propagation through validation, deterministic state execution, and finality confirmation. It includes parallelisation strategies, layer-2 scaling (state channels, rollups), and cross-chain atomic operations, with MEV mitigation and encrypted mempools addressing ordering fairness.",
